 "note": "Dungeon loot tables (core/game/game_dungeon_loot.gd, checked by tools/check_data.gd). `GameDungeonLoot.roll(d, dungeon, container, tier)` is a pure function of the seed, the dungeon, the container and the 'cycle' (how many `refill_years` of the world's calendar have passed), never the dynasty's dice. A `tier` of container says how many rolls it gives (`rolls`), the chance of each being a made item (`item_chance`; else a find of materials), the gold (`gold`, scaled by the generation), a `rarity_boost` on the rare rarities, and the lowest rarity it can give (`min_rarity`). Items are built by GameLoot's own parts (forms, materials, affixes, rarities): the generation opens material tiers and adds grades. Each dungeon's table then weights the slot (`slot_weights`), the forms (`form_bias`) and the materials by their tags (`material_tag_bias`), lifts the material ceiling by `tier_shift`, scales gold by `gold_mult`, lists the `materials` its rooms hold, its `uniques` (named items of items.json, one each for a dynasty, in a container of a room `role`) and what its creatures `drops`. The room's depth (doors from the entrance) raises the rarity boost by `depth_boost` a door. A container `kind` may shift the slots (`slot_mult`) or the gold (`gold_mult`).",
